            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0503" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12/1765: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hawks</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-16T12:00:00-05:00">March 16, 1934—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Your cables No. 23, March 14, 5 p.m., and No. 24, March 15, 10 a.m.<anchor
                        n="55" xml:id="d437-f1"/> Department considering suggested changes but
                    desires <pb facs="0504" n="438" xml:id="pg438"/> clarification of specific
                    change for page 8. It is meaningless to insert “and reply brief” after “answer”
                    in the two lines mentioned in your cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
